              "Management"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "knowledge": {
        "decision_rule": "Step-wise approach to asthma management with SABA as needed for mild intermittent asthma, adding ICS for persistent asthma, and LABA/ICS combinations for moderate to severe asthma.",
        "guideline_ref": {
          "name": "BTS/SIGN",
          "year": 2019,
          "key_line": "For adults with asthma, offer a SABA as reliever therapy and a low dose ICS as first-line maintenance therapy."
        },
        "misconceptions": [
          "All asthma patients need daily inhaled corticosteroids",
          "Salbutamol can be used indefinitely without controller therapy",
          "Oral steroids are first-line for mild asthma exacerbations",
          "Antibiotics are routinely indicated for asthma exacerbations"
        ]
      },
